<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43719" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔεδρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on stately throne</i>, of gods, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				96
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				319
			</span></i> (both lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. καθέδρα</span>
			<i>a firm</i> seat on horseback, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.21
			</span></i>; <i>well-poised</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				157.3
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρως</span>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεβαίως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of ships, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰσσελμος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				13.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>well-fitting</i>, of building materials, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρως</span>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθέτως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>easy to sit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>in a right</i> or <i>lucky place</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔεδρος ὄρνις</span> a bird of augury <i>appearing in a
				lucky quarter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				16.16
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
